From b6e0b54036ae5b1ba3b6f5fb4681da7a321dcbdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eddy Sangalli <eddyrodrigues@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:11:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(overlays): build Downstream Keyer in-tree, fix
 uninitialised hide-after

Downstream Keyer 0.4.4 by Exeldro (GPL-2.0) is now built as part of FreeMix
from plugins/downstream-keyer instead of being shipped as a separate binary.

Changes to the upstream code:
- DownstreamKeyer::hideAfter starts at zero. Upstream left it uninitialised,
  so a keyer created at run time took whatever was in memory as its "hide
  after" time, saved it with the scene collection and, on the next start,
  dropped its scene right after showing it (overlays that would not stay on,
  audio bus scene going off air).
- New vendor request "dsk_set_hide_after" { dsk_name, hide_after } in
  milliseconds, for the duration of an overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
